# Tavily Docs

- [Connect your AI agent to the web](https://docs.tavily.com/index.md): Add Tavily's web search, extraction, crawling, and research to Claude, Codex, Cursor, or any agent in one step, or call the API directly with a free API key.
- [Tavily MCP](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/mcp.md): Connect Tavily's search, extract, crawl, map, and research tools to Claude, ChatGPT, Codex, Cursor, VS Code, or any MCP client.
- [Tavily Agent Skills](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/agent-skills.md): Official skills that define best practices, adding web search, extraction, crawling, and research to any AI coding agent.
- [Claude](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/claude.md): Add Tavily web search, extraction, crawling, and research to Claude Code, claude.ai, and Claude Desktop.
- [Tavily CLI](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/tavily-cli.md): Search, extract, crawl, map, and research the web from your terminal.
- [Quickstart](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/python/quick-start.md): Integrate Tavily's powerful APIs natively in your Python apps.
- [Quickstart](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/javascript/quick-start.md): Integrate Tavily's powerful APIs natively in your JavaScript/TypeScript projects.
- [Claude Code](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/claude-code.md): Add Tavily web search, extraction, crawling, and research to Claude Code with the official Tavily plugin.
- [Codex](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/codex.md): Add Tavily web search, extraction, crawling, and research to Codex with the official Tavily plugin or MCP server.
- [Cursor](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/cursor.md): Add Tavily web search, extraction, crawling, and research to Cursor in one click.
- [Kiro](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/kiro.md): Add Tavily web search, extraction, crawling, and research to Kiro through the Tavily MCP server.
- [Kilo](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/kilo.md): Add Tavily web search, extraction, crawling, and research to Kilo through the Tavily MCP server.
- [OpenCode](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/opencode.md): Add real-time web search, extraction, crawling, and deep research to OpenCode, the open-source terminal coding agent, through the official opencode-tavily plugin.
- [Hermes Agent](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/hermes-agent.md): Use Tavily in Hermes Agent through the Tavily plugin or as the built-in web backend.
- [Pi](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/pi.md): Use Tavily in Pi via the official @tavily/pi-extension package to add web search and page extraction tools to your coding agent workflow.
- [NanoClaw](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/nanoclaw.md): Add Tavily Search and Extract to a persistent NanoClaw agent in Slack, Telegram, Discord, or the CLI.
- [OpenClaw](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/openclaw.md): Integrate Tavily with OpenClaw to give your AI agents real-time web search and content extraction across WhatsApp, Telegram, Discord, iMessage, and more.
- [Grok Build](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/grok-build.md): Add real-time web search, extraction, crawling, and deep research to Grok Build, xAI's terminal coding agent, through the official Tavily plugin.
- [Replit](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/replit.md): Add Tavily web search, extraction, crawling, and research to Replit through the Tavily MCP server.
- [Try Tavily Without an API Key](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/keyless.md): Use Tavily Search and Extract for free, with zero setup. No account, no API key, no configuration. Keyless responses are identical to keyed responses.
- [API Key Management](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/best-practices/api-key-management.md): Learn how to handle API key leaks and best practices for key rotation.
- [Organizations and workspaces](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/platform/managing-organizations.md): Organize an account into workspaces, each with its own members, API keys, and credit limit, while billing stays with the organization.
- [Headers & Authentication](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-headers.md): Base URL, authentication, and optional request headers for the Tavily API.
- [Credits & Pricing](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-credits.md): Learn how to get and manage your Tavily API Credits.
- [Rate Limits](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/rate-limits.md): Learn about Tavily's API rate limits for both  development and production environments.
- [Best Practices for Search](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/best-practices/best-practices-search.md): Optimize individual queries, and run search reliably at scale with batch workflows.
- [Best Practices for Extract](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/best-practices/best-practices-extract.md): Learn how to optimize content extraction, choose the right approach, and configure parameters for better performance.
- [Best Practices for Crawl](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/best-practices/best-practices-crawl.md): Learn how to optimize crawl parameters, focus your crawls, and efficiently extract content from websites.
- [Best Practices for Research](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/best-practices/best-practices-research.md): Learn how to write effective prompts, choose the right model, and configure output formats for better research results.
- [Tavily Knowledge - Company](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/best-practices/company-data.md): Get company records for 35M+ companies worldwide in /search and /extract results.
- [Frequently Asked Questions](https://docs.tavily.com/faq/faq.md)
- [Help Center](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/help.md)
- [Tavily Search](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-reference/endpoint/search.md): Execute a search query using Tavily Search.
- [Tavily Extract](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-reference/endpoint/extract.md): Extract content from one URL or batch up to 20 URLs in one request. Successful URLs appear in results; per-URL failures appear in failed_results. Check both arrays even when the response is HTTP 200. Request options apply to every URL in the batch.
- [Tavily Crawl](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-reference/endpoint/crawl.md): Tavily Crawl is a graph-based website traversal tool that can explore hundreds of paths in parallel with built-in extraction and intelligent discovery.
- [Tavily Map](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-reference/endpoint/map.md): Tavily Map traverses websites like a graph and can explore hundreds of paths in parallel with intelligent discovery to generate comprehensive site maps.
- [Create Research Task](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-reference/endpoint/research.md): Tavily Research performs comprehensive research on a given topic by conducting multiple searches, analyzing sources, and generating a detailed research report.
- [Get Research Task Status](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-reference/endpoint/research-get.md): Retrieve the status and results of a research task using its request ID.
- [Streaming](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-reference/endpoint/research-streaming.md): Stream real-time research progress and results from Tavily Research API
- [Feedback](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-reference/endpoint/feedback.md): Submit feedback on how relevant and useful Tavily's results were for your task.
- [Usage](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-reference/endpoint/usage.md): Get API key and account usage details
- [Logs](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/api-reference/endpoint/logs.md): Retrieve per-request usage logs for the API keys under your account or organization.
- [Generate Keys](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/enterprise/generate-keys.md): Generate one or more API keys with custom configuration.
- [Deactivate Keys](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/enterprise/deactivate-keys.md): Deactivate API keys either in bulk by `request_id` or individually.
- [Key Info](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/enterprise/key-info.md): Get information about an API key. The key to query is specified in the `Authorization` header.
- [Organization Usage](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/enterprise/org-usage.md): Retrieve usage (credits), pay-as-you-go USD cost, and request counts for **every API key under an organization you own**, mirroring the platform's Usage analytics page.
- [SDK Reference](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/python/reference.md): Integrate Tavily's powerful APIs natively in your Python apps.
- [SDK Reference](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/javascript/reference.md): Integrate Tavily's powerful APIs natively in your JavaScript/TypeScript projects.
- [Integrations](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/overview.md): Connect Tavily to your framework, platform, gateway, or cloud. Pick an integration to get started.
- [Merge Gateway](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/merge-gateway.md): Use Tavily as the search engine behind Merge Gateway's web search tool, so any model routed through Gateway can answer with current, cited web results.
- [Eden AI](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/eden-ai.md): Run Tavily Search through Eden AI's unified API by selecting Tavily as the web search provider.
- [Composio](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/composio.md): Use Tavily with Claude, Codex, and other agents through Composio Instant or your own API key, for personal and team workflows.
- [Arcade.dev](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/arcade-dev.md): Connect Tavily to Arcade.dev MCP Gateway for governed web search, extraction, crawling, mapping, and research.
- [Scalekit](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/scalekit.md): Connect AI agents to Tavily's MCP server through Scalekit AgentKit.
- [TrueFoundry](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/truefoundry.md): Connect Tavily as a managed MCP server through the TrueFoundry MCP Gateway.
- [LangChain](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/langchain.md): We're excited to partner with Langchain as their recommended search tool!
- [OpenAI](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/openai.md): Integrate Tavily with OpenAI to enhance your AI applications with real-time web search capabilities.
- [n8n](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/n8n.md): Use Tavily in n8n workflows and AI Agents to search the web, extract page content, crawl and map websites, and run research, without writing code.
- [Vercel AI SDK](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/vercel.md): Integrate Tavily with Vercel AI SDK to enhance your AI agents with powerful web search, content extraction, crawling, and site mapping capabilities.
- [Vercel Connect](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/vercel-connect.md): Connect Tavily to Vercel apps and agents with managed OAuth or API keys, then search through MCP, REST, or Eve.
- [Anthropic](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/anthropic.md): Integrate Tavily with Anthropic Claude to enhance your AI applications with real-time web search capabilities.
- [Microsoft 365 Copilot](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/microsoft.md): Use Tavily as a declarative agent in Microsoft 365 Copilot or as a plugin in Copilot Cowork for real-time web search, extraction, mapping, and crawling.
- [Google Gemini Enterprise](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/google-gemini-enterprise.md): Connect Tavily to Google Gemini Enterprise for web search, content extraction, crawling, and research.
- [Devin](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/devin.md): Connect Tavily to Devin through the MCP Marketplace so Devin can search the web, read docs, and ground coding tasks with live web context.
- [Dify](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/dify.md): Tavily is now available for no-code integration through Dify.
- [Make](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/make.md): Tavily is now available for no-code integration through Make.
- [Agno](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/agno.md): Tavily is now available for integration through Agno.
- [Cartesia](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/cartesia.md): Build real-time voice agents that search and extract web content with Tavily and the Cartesia Line SDK.
- [Convex](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/convex.md): Add real-time web search and content extraction to your Convex application with the official Tavily Convex component.
- [CrewAI](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/crewai.md): Integrate Tavily with CrewAI to build powerful AI agents that can search the web.
- [ElevenLabs](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/elevenlabs.md): Connect Tavily to ElevenLabs ElevenAgents so your agents can use live web search.
- [Factory AI](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/factory-ai.md): Connect Tavily to Factory's Droid to search the web and use current sources in coding tasks.
- [FlowiseAI](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/flowise.md): Tavily is now available for integration through Flowise.
- [Gradium](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/gradium.md): Use Tavily web search with Gradium voice AI agents.
- [Haystack](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/haystack.md): Use Tavily inside Haystack pipelines with the `tavily-haystack` integration.
- [Langflow](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/langflow.md): Integrate Tavily with Langflow, an open-source visual framework for building multi-agent and RAG applications.
- [Langfuse](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/langfuse.md): Trace and observe Tavily Search and Extract calls inside your LLM applications with Langfuse.
- [LibreChat](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/librechat.md): Use Tavily inside LibreChat for web search, content extraction, and as a built-in agent tool.
- [LlamaIndex](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/llamaindex.md): Search the web from LlamaIndex with Tavily.
- [Mastra](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/mastra.md): Use Tavily as first-class Mastra tools for web search, extract, crawl, and map via the native package.
- [Nemo Deep Agents](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/nemo-deepagents.md): Enable Tavily for NVIDIA NemoClaw's nemo-deepagents sandbox so LangChain Deep Agents Code can use web search and extraction through governed OpenShell egress.
- [OpenAI Agent Builder](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/agent-builder.md): Integrate OpenAI’s Agent Builder with Tavily’s MCP server to empower your AI agents with real-time web access.
- [Portkey](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/portkey.md): Use Tavily with Portkey either through the Tavily MCP server or the Tavily Online Search plugin.
- [Pydantic AI](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/pydantic-ai.md): Tavily is now available for integration through Pydantic AI.
- [Ramp Glass](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/ramp-glass.md): Connect Tavily to Ramp Glass for web research, with organization-level availability and personal account setup.
- [StackAI](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/stackai.md): Using Tavily in StackAI to enhance your AI workflows with real-time web data.
- [Tines](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/tines.md): Integrate Tavily with Tines for automated, no-code intelligence workflows.
- [Vellum](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/vellum.md): Use Tavily as the built-in web search provider in the Vellum Assistant desktop app.
- [Workato](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/workato.md): Connect Tavily to Workato recipes for web search, content extraction, crawling, mapping, and research.
- [Zapier](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/integrations/zapier.md): Tavily is now available for no-code integration through Zapier.
- [Databricks](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/partnerships/databricks.md): Integrate Tavily MCP Server with Databricks for real-time web search and RAG capabilities.
- [Amazon Bedrock AgentCore](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/partnerships/amazon.md): Integrate Tavily MCP Server with Amazon Bedrock AgentCore for scalable AI agent deployment on AWS.
- [Microsoft Azure](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/partnerships/azure.md): Integrate Tavily Remote MCP with Microsoft Azure AI Foundry and Azure MCP Center for seamless AI agent development.
- [IBM watsonx Orchestrate](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/partnerships/ibm.md): Integrate Tavily's AI-powered research capabilities with IBM watsonx Orchestrate
- [Snowflake](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/partnerships/snowflake.md): Tavily is now available as a native app on the [Snowflake Marketplace](https://app.snowflake.com/marketplace/listing/GZTSZ2XM0ON/tavily-tavily-search-api?search=tavily).
- [Tavily x402](https://docs.tavily.com/documentation/machine-payments/x402.md): AI agents pay per request for Tavily Advanced Search in USDC on Base — no API key, no account, no human in the loop.
- [Examples Hub](https://docs.tavily.com/examples/hub.md): Build with Tavily — from quick API recipes to production research agents.
- [Chat](https://docs.tavily.com/examples/use-cases/chat.md): A conversational AI agent using Tavily Search to answer questions with web sources.
- [Supply Chain Risk Research](https://docs.tavily.com/examples/use-cases/supply-chain-risk.md): Research suppliers with Tavily to uncover business risks, disruptions, and official risk signals.
- [Data Enrichment](https://docs.tavily.com/examples/use-cases/data-enrichment.md): Fill spreadsheet cells with current web research and source links using Tavily.
- [Company Research](https://docs.tavily.com/examples/use-cases/company-research.md): Research a company's business, industry, financial context, and recent news with Tavily.
- [Sales Meeting Preparation](https://docs.tavily.com/examples/use-cases/meeting-prep.md): A sales research workflow using Tavily to prepare company context, recent developments, and conversation starters.
- [Financial Market Research](https://docs.tavily.com/examples/use-cases/market-researcher.md): Research portfolio stocks with Tavily for a quick overview or a detailed report.
- [Financial Services & Insurance Kit](https://docs.tavily.com/examples/use-cases/fsi-kit.md): Research compliance risk, investments, merchants, and insurance applicants with Tavily.
- [Slack Research Agent](https://docs.tavily.com/examples/use-cases/slack-research-agent.md): A research Slack agent backed by a LangChain Deep Agent, with Tavily search and extract as tools.
- [Projects](https://docs.tavily.com/examples/open-sources/projects.md): Explore our collection of popular open source projects that showcase Tavily's use cases and capabilities.
- [Changelog](https://docs.tavily.com/changelog.md): New features and updates to the Tavily API, SDKs, and platform.

